======================================================================
1. HOW THIS REVIEW WAS DONE
======================================================================

I read the full difference between the run-2 file and the run-3 file, then read the new
functions in place. Every one of the 127 rows was read against its Expected Result and Test
Result Criteria. I could not call the model from this workspace (the connection to the model
provider is refused), so I did not re-run chat questions. Where the Actual Result was enough I
graded from it. Where I could check something myself against the real corpus text (the
text cache, now 18,355,857 characters after extraction repair) or the submitted code, I did,
and column J says so. Checks I ran myself, without the model:

  - cache similarity of the TC-045 paraphrase pair under the new tokenizer       TC-045
  - _quoted_spans on the TC-030 answer text, ellipsis splitting, attribution note  TC-030, 014, 108
  - answer_items, _has_own_topic and _contextual_retrieval_query on the follow-up
    questions                                                                       TC-026, 059, 069, 111
  - retrieve_chunks for the sanitized TC-035 and TC-096 prompts                      TC-035, 096
  - catalog_answer on topic-plus-year questions                                      TC-046
  - corpus counts by content year, distinct works, duplicate groups                  TC-025, 088, 091
  - extraction repair effect on the character total                                  TC-072
  - usage message and exit codes for an unknown mode                                 TC-125
  - the fix checks inside the submission (_review_fix_checks), about 50 lines         TC-069

Result values used: Pass, Fail, Blocked, Not Run. A harness result was overridden where my
evidence disagreed: TC-035 and TC-054 (harness Pass, graded Fail), TC-072 and TC-119
(harness Fail, graded Pass because the workbook expectation is out of date). TC-107 and
TC-125 were not decided by the harness; I checked them and graded Pass. No credentials were
used or stored in any file.


