======================================================================
3. CONFORMANCE TO THE SPECIFICATION
======================================================================

Overall: all six features in spec section 6 are implemented. Four are met in behaviour; 6.2
(follow-ups) is worse than in run 2 because of a new rule, and 6.6 (quotation support) still
has faults in the counting.

6.1 Conversational loop ........................ MET
    Unknown command-line mode now prints a usage message and exits with code 2 (TC-125,
    checked by me). /exit, /quit, /sources, /help, EOF and empty input are clean. Ctrl-C
    on the terminal was not pressed by hand (TC-065 Not Run).

6.2 Session memory for follow-ups .............. PARTLY MET (regressed)
    Ordered items are now stored and "the first one" style questions can be resolved
    (F-03 work), but two new defects break the common cases: "What year was that paper
    published?" and "And who wrote that one?" are refused (TC-059, 069, 111), and "the second
    one" after a year-led timeline picks a paper that was not in the answer (TC-026). See N-02.

6.3 Publication-year extraction and trend ...... MET for year and order, PARTLY for relevance
    Years now come from the content when the filename year is contradicted by the first page
    (14 files). Trend items are sorted by year before the model sees them (_prepare_items,
    design 4.5 now met). Trend answers are in order (TC-020 Pass). The relevance gate is too
    weak: loosely related passages still produce an invented story (TC-089, TC-019).

6.4 Reader-facing citations .................... MET with small gaps
    The same paper is no longer listed twice, "[paper: ... | year: ...]" tags are rewritten,
    and Sources is dropped or labelled "retrieved, not used" on refusals. Remaining: nine
    volume files still get file-name labels, one title is a garbled author line, one answer
    shows a raw DBLP id in prose, and the Sources dedupe can drop the label that the text
    cited (TC-021, 068). See N-12, N-13, N-15.

6.5 Structured comparison answers .............. PARTLY MET
    Comparisons with both sides present work. A comparison where one side is missing from
    the retrieved passages is refused as a whole (TC-015, 084, 085). See N-03.

6.6 Direct-quotation support made visible ...... PARTLY MET
    Line breaks in the extracted text no longer cause false negatives, titles are skipped,
    and the check now lists which papers contain the quote. The span finder still pairs the
    quote characters wrongly after a short quoted word, and ellipses split a real quote into
    two parts that are scored as separate failures (TC-030, TC-014, TC-108). See N-04.

7. What does not change ........................ MET
    Injection handling holds (TC-036 to 040, 070, 097 to 102). The fuzzy cache works for
    exact repeats but no longer for the TC-045 paraphrase (N-01).

10. Known limitations .......................... CONFIRMED
    Filename-based years are now partly replaced by content years. New limitation seen in
    this run: the lexical retriever cannot tell that a conference copy and a preprint copy of
    one work are the same work unless told (N-07).


