5B. NEW FINDINGS IN RUN 3

N-01  Fuzzy cache no longer matches a close paraphrase  [Major]  TC-045, warm benchmark
      The tokenizer keeps two-character tokens now, so "Tell me the main idea..." adds "me" to the
      token set. Jaccard overlap falls from 6/7 (0.857) to 6/8 (0.75), under the 0.8 threshold. The
      warm benchmark pass makes model calls for two of three paraphrases.
      Fix: build the cache key with its own helper that ignores tokens of two characters or fewer and
      a short filler list (tell, me, please, give, show, explain, describe, say). Add the TC-045 pair
      to the conv-check.

N-02  Follow-up logic fails on simple follow-ups  [Blocking]  TC-026, 059, 069, 111
      _has_own_topic treats any two content words as a topic, so "What year was that paper
      published?" (year, published) and "And who wrote that one?" (wrote, one) are called
      self-contained and the previous paper is not added to the query. answer_items returns
      ["2022-2025"] for a bullet list that starts with years, so "the second one" cannot be resolved.
      Fix: test for an anaphora word first (that, this, it, its, they, those, "the first/second/last
      one", "same paper"); if present, always add the previous paper. Make answer_items skip a leading
      year and take the title or label that follows it. Add the three questions to the conv-check.

N-03  Comparison with one missing side refuses everything  [Blocking]  TC-015, 084, 085
      When the passages cover only one of the two things compared, the model answers "the documents do
      not cover X" and describes neither. Fix: add a rule to the compare addendum (describe the side
      that was found, say which was not found), and for "X and Y" questions retrieve once per side.

N-04  Quotation support counts wrongly  [Major]  TC-030, 014, 108
      _quoted_spans pairs the closing quote of a short quoted word with the next opening quote and
      returns the text between them as a "quote". A real sentence is then not counted (0/4 for a
      verified sentence). Ellipses split one real quote into two parts, giving 2/3.
      Fix: pair quote characters left to right, then filter by length (20 or more characters); split
      on "..." and the ellipsis character and check each part of 20 or more characters.

N-05  _is_refusal false positives and misses  [Minor]  TC-017, 029, 086
      Answers that contain "do not cover" inside a useful sentence are treated as refusals, and
      answers such as "was not retrieved" are not. Fix: test only the first sentence, and add the
      "was not retrieved / not found in the collection" wordings.

N-06  Retrieval junk after the sanitizer removes a block  [Major]  TC-035, 096
      The lead-in "Using the e-mails as context" is stemmed to "e-mail" after the generic-word
      filter, so editors' e-mail lines in proceedings front matter score 22 to 27 against 15 for the
      sketching papers. The model then refuses a sketching question that the sanitizer left intact.
      Fix: apply the generic-word filter to the stemmed term as well, add e-mail words to it, and
      when the sanitizer removed a block, drop the lead-in clause before retrieval.

N-07  Duplicate and preprint copies not explained to the model  [Major]  TC-054, 022, 021, 058
      Aliases are collapsed in the index but the model is not told that a work exists under several
      file names. TC-054 invents a "journal version" with its own numbers. TC-022 writes a paper as
      the follow-up of itself. Fix: in the turn rules, name the aliases of each retrieved work and
      tell the model they are one work; in trend intent group by normalized title before the prompt.

N-08  Trend relevance gate too weak  [Blocking]  TC-089, 019
      A passage passes if it contains any topic word, so "sketch recognition research" is written
      from RNN, CAD and program-sketch papers. Fix: require every distinctive topic term (or two of
      them), count distinct dated works that pass, and if fewer than three return a fixed "too few
      papers" reply without a model call. For two year ranges in one question, retrieve once per range.

N-09  Catalog route takes topic-plus-year questions  [Minor]  TC-046
      A question such as "papers on sketching in 2016" is answered by counting 2016 papers. Fix:
      route to the catalog only when the question has no topic term besides year words.

N-10  Question that names a proceedings volume gets nothing  [Major]  TC-057
      The volume cap (budget 1, factor 0.8, chunks with n=1 excluded) also blocks a question that
      names "CAV 2021 proceedings volume". Fix: if the question matches a volume label, retrieve up to
      four chunks from that volume with no penalty.

N-11  Bibliographic questions answered from reference lists  [Major]  TC-008
      "What year / which conference was X published" is answered from a citation in another paper
      (ASPLOS 2006 instead of PLDI 2005). Fix: answer from metadata (display_label plus venue parsed
      from the id) without a model call, and add a prompt rule that a paper's year is the year
      attribute of its own passage tag.

N-12  File-name or garbled labels remain  [Minor]  TC-068
      Nine files whose id ends in _YYYY (aplas_2009, cav_2011, cav_2012, cav_2015, hvc_2012,
      ppsn_2014, sat_2012, sat_2016, vmcai_2014) are shown by file name, and one title is an author
      line ("Kevin Ellis*..."). Fix: treat those ids as volumes and add display-title overrides.

N-13  sources_block title-key dedupe can drop the cited label  [Minor]  TC-021, 068
      When two ids share a title key, the one kept may not be the one cited inline. Fix: keep the id
      that the answer cited, then the first.

N-14  BASELINE_MAX_TOKENS below the observed BEFORE pass  [Minor]  TC-050, benchmark
      The constant is 1,100,000; the BEFORE pass used about 1.17M tokens, so the drift flag still
      prints. Fix: set it from the measured pass with a margin, for example 1,400,000.

N-15  Raw DBLP id in prose  [Minor]  TC-058
      "DBLP_conf_cav_..." appears in the answer text. Fix: have rewrite_inline_citations replace any
      bare corpus id with its display label.

N-16  Workbook and harness items  [see section 6 and 7]  TC-035, 054, 072, 119, 025, 088, 091, 050

Positive controls for the recording: TC-001, 009, 020, 027, 029, 036 to 040, 044, 070,
078, 092, 093, 094, 125.


